From b5f8dbbb42d1733952dc0fb7e23d6790554c3e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:37:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-oneplus-hotdog: restore the
 DisplayPort alt mode

The USB-C connector lost its altmodes node in the 6.17 reconstruction, so
the port registered no alternate mode at all. /sys/class/typec then holds
only port0 and port0-partner: the partner advertises SVID ff01 and PD
negotiates fine, but with nothing on the port side to enter the mode the
DisplayPort connector stays disconnected and no video ever leaves the
phone.

The dock enumerates its hub, its Realtek ethernet and its mass storage
perfectly, which is what makes this look like a display problem rather
than a missing description.

Same node as sm8150-hdk and qrb5165-rb5, and the same one this board
carried on 6.16, where DisplayPort worked on this dock.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
index 750dc631e1089..f4ed8ed75e6c1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -999,6 +999,13 @@ PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
 				       PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 		op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
 
+		altmodes {
+			displayport {
+				svid = /bits/ 16 <0xff01>;
+				vdo = <0x00001c46>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
